# AI pipeline

All LLM work goes through `core/ai/llm_router.py`, `core/ai/llm_client.py`, and `core/ai/validators.py`. Routes, services, and the frontend do not call a provider SDK directly.

Order: preprocess, detect intent, choose a model, call the model, postprocess, validate the schema, log latency and cost, return the structured result.

- The API result is the schema, not free text.
- Set a temperature bound and `max_tokens`. Truncate long threads before the call.
- Retry provider failures with exponential backoff and jitter, and log the failure.
- Do not run a model over a whole table or a long mailbox in one call.
- Keep the pipeline linear. Pass a summary into the next step when the full output is not required.
- Log `latency_ms` and `cost_usd` when the call reports them. Do not log the raw prompt or response when it holds personal data.

Read `.cursor/rules/email.mdc` when the call classifies or replies to mail.
